From: mocha port <local>
Subject: [PATCH 0006] hwui: preload EGL on the RenderThread instead of a detached thread

Taken from the validated r15 work on the Abobo7 lineage-17.1 tree ("EGL preload
lifetime repairs"). RenderProxy already posts preload() to the RenderThread, so
spawning a detached thread for eglGetDisplay(EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY) only creates a
race: the stock Tegra 334.00 EGL driver keeps display/client state in library
globals, and the short-lived thread's exit (implicit eglReleaseThread) can tear
that state down while the RenderThread is in the middle of its first
eglGetDisplay()/eglInitialize(). Do the preload inline.
---
diff --git a/libs/hwui/renderthread/RenderThread.cpp b/libs/hwui/renderthread/RenderThread.cpp
index f83c0a4926f9..c3c3f7cc9736 100644
--- a/libs/hwui/renderthread/RenderThread.cpp
+++ b/libs/hwui/renderthread/RenderThread.cpp
@@ -477,8 +477,14 @@ bool RenderThread::isCurrent() {
 void RenderThread::preload() {
     // EGL driver is always preloaded only if HWUI renders with GL.
     if (Properties::getRenderPipelineType() == RenderPipelineType::SkiaGL) {
-        std::thread eglInitThread([]() { eglGetDisplay(EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY); });
-        eglInitThread.detach();
+        // preload() ya se envia por RenderProxy a ESTE hilo. Los drivers EGL
+        // legacy (Tegra 334.00) guardan el estado de display/global por proceso
+        // dentro de la propia libreria: un hilo suelto de preload llama a
+        // eglGetDisplay() en paralelo con el eglGetDisplay()/eglInitialize() del
+        // primer frame y, al terminar, puede derribar ese estado compartido
+        // (eglReleaseThread implicito en el exit de hilo). Hacerlo inline evita la
+        // carrera en la primera frame.
+        eglGetDisplay(EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY);
     } else {
         requireVkContext();
     }
